Liskov Substitution Principle

      Subclasses should be replaceable without breaking behavior
      Derived classes should be replaceable for their base classes without breaking functionality.
      
      Wherever a parent object is expected, a child object should work safely.

Bad Example

        class Vehicle:
            def start_engine(self):
                pass
                
        class Bicycle(Vehicle):
            def start_engine(self):
                raise Exception("No engine")

Good Example
          class Vehicle:
              pass

          class Bicycle(Vehicle):
              pass

          class EngineVehicle(Vehicle):
              def start_engine(self):
                  pass
          
          class Car(EngineVehicle):
              pass
          
          
